    "https://careers.mtsu.edu/jobs/associate-athletic-trainer-murfreesboro-tennessee-tennessee-united-states-1af3cdc2-f794-4914-bf67-5d9955c612a6": {
      "title": "Associate Athletic Trainer*",
      "description": "Associate Athletic Trainer* - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Visit MTSU Why Choose MTSU Applicant Log In My Profile Kiosk mode Associate Athletic Trainer* 498657 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Athletics and Coaching Administrative Add to favorites View favorites Job Title Associate Athletic Trainer Department Athletic Trainer Salary Commensurate with experience Job Summary/Basic Function The Associate Athletic Trainer will report to the Associate Athletic Director of Sports Medicine. The position will supervise and coordinate athletic training services for student-athletes in intercollegiate athletic programs – men's and women's cross country, men’s and women’s track and field, and secondary sport responsibilities as needed. Essential duties include but are not be limited to: collecting pre-participation medical paperwork, organizing and scheduling pre-participation physical exams, assist with the prevention, treatment, rehabilitation, physician referral, and medical documentation of all injuries associated with assigned student athletes; design and implement rehabilitation plan; establishing criteria for safe return to practice and play and implementing the return to play process; communicate with coaches, student athletes, parents, staff and physicians within NATA and HIPAA guidelines; observe all athletic policy and procedures in accordance with NATA regulations as well as NCAA, Conference USA and MTSU rules and remain certified to perform these duties on a daily basis. Coordinate Concussion testing and baseline testing for all assigned student-athletes; provide supervision of daily practice and game coverage, in-season travel, and summer sports workout coverage for assigned student-athletes as permitted by NCAA legislation. This position must be flexible, adapt to schedule changes as necessary, and serve as an approved preceptor within the CAATE-accredited graduate athletic training program. Provide direct supervision of intern athletic trainers, graduate athletic training students in the athletic training education program, and undergraduate student assistants assigned to football and/or other sports, as assigned; instruct these students in professional prevention, care, and rehabilitation of assigned student-athletes and the certification and licensure process. Required to attend national NATA and Conference USA meetings and/or conventions to remain current in their field for changes that occur; comply with NCAA, CAATE, and NATA legislation, and immediately report any known violations of any of these rules to the Compliance office and submit all required documentation to the Compliance office immediately. The Associate Athletic Trainer will assist with coordinating the drug testing/educational program for all student-athletes and perform other related tasks or special projects as assigned. Required Education Bachelor’s Degree required. Master's Degree preferred. Required Related Experience Two (2) years of progressively responsible, relevant collegiate and/or clinical athletic training experience. Graduate Assistant experience will be accepted. Required License/Registration/Certification NATA BOC Certification and Tennessee State Licensure, or eligible for Tennessee State Licensure. Knowledge of NCAA, CUSA & NATABOC rules and regulations required. CPR, AED, and First Aid Certification required. Desirable Related Experience Four (4) years of progressively responsible Division I Athletic Training Desirable License/Registration/Certification CES, CSCS, PES, Dry Needling Preferred Documents Needed to Apply Resume Required MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee and their spouse and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email hrs@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: For best consideration, pleay apply by August 10, 2026.  Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and the position may be filled before the listed application review date of October 8, 2026*. Recommended Jobs Academic Advisor/Advanced Academic Advisor -  College of Basic and Applied Sciences (CBAS) Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Academic Advising , College of Basic & Applied Sciences The College of Basic and Applied Sciences (CBAS) at Middle Tennessee State University invites applications for an Academic Advisor/Advanced Academic Advisor position in the following departments: Department of Aerospace, School of Agriculture, Department of Chemistry and Pre-Professional Health Sciences, Department of Computational and Data Science, and the School of Concrete and Construction Management. The Academic Advisor will collaborate with students to co-create educational plans in ways that are consistent with their aspirations, interests, strengths, and values--preparing them for a life of learning in a diverse and global society. MTSU Academic Advising fosters a collaborative, holistic, and inclusive student-centered relationship that promotes academic and personal growth so students can thrive in the University community. Through innovative, transformative, and informed practice, Academic Advisors empower students to think critically and take ownership of their journey and success. Academic Advisors work with traditional, transfer, undeclared, and pre-professional health students, ensuring they stay on track for graduation through constant engagement and monitoring. The Academic Advisor role is geared toward supporting student success, providing both academic and career advising while maintaining high standards of professionalism and collaboration within their respective college. CBAS has an established Advising Center with high professional standards and a reputation for excellence. The best qualified candidate is student-centered, communicates clearly and effectively, is a team player, advocates for STEM, and is capable of working effectively with staff and faculty to serve the diverse needs of students.\n\nThe Advanced Academic Advisor builds upon the foundational role of the Academic Advisor, offering deeper expertise in academic planning, student engagement, and retention strategies. This position focuses on providing enhanced advising services to specialized student populations, including transfer students, at-risk students, and those in specific academic disciplines. The Advanced Advisor works closely with faculty and administrative staff to ensure that students meet academic goals and are on track for graduation. The role also includes involvement in professional development and special projects that contribute to the overall success of the advising center. Perform related tasks and special projects as assigned. Note: a flexible work schedule is required to accommodate student requests for advising after traditional work hours. Maintenance Supervisor - TN Miller Coliseum Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Facilities Services - Maintenance, Other Perform a variety of repair and preventative maintenance tasks including electrical, plumbing, HVAC, carpentry, metal fabrication, and masonry for the Tennessee Miller Coliseum. Operate HVAC system controls to ensure appropriate cooling or heating of indoor spaces. Arrange and oversee maintenance service from external contractors or other university departments. Train, schedule, and supervise part-time maintenance staff. Perform other tasks as assigned. Administrative Assistant 3 - Joey A. Jacobs Chair of Excellence in Accounting Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Administrative/Clerical Support, College of Business The Administrative Assistant 3 provides comprehensive administrative, operational, and event-planning support to the Joey A. Jacobs Chair of Excellence in Accounting within the Department of Accounting at Middle Tennessee State University (MTSU). The position helps advance the Chair’s mission of promoting leadership in accounting education, professional engagement, student development, and outreach through programs, events, and collaborations with internal and external stakeholders.\n\nKey responsibilities include planning and coordinating conferences, workshops, meetings, and special events; assisting with marketing and promotional activities; managing social media communications; arranging travel, catering, room reservations, and event logistics; and coordinating the selection and ordering of awards, gifts, promotional items, and memorabilia. The role also maintains records, registrations, rosters, and electronic files; prepares reports and correspondence; and provides administrative support for academic and program initiatives.\n\nThe position serves as a central point of contact for the Jacobs Chair, working closely with faculty, students, Beta Alpha Psi, professional accounting organizations, industry representatives, government agencies, educational institutions, and other partners. Responsibilities include facilitating communications, coordinating activities among stakeholders, addressing operational issues, and supporting initiatives that increase the visibility and impact of MTSU’s accounting program. The Administrative Assistant also assists with academic and administrative processes and performs other duties necessary to support the goals and activities of the Jacobs Chair of Excellence. © 2026 Middle Tennessee State University Cookie Preferences Nondiscrimination Policy Terms Follow Us: Facebook LinkedIn X Instagram Youtube Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
