ent success, providing both academic and career advising while maintaining high standards of professionalism and collaboration within their respective college. CBAS has an established Advising Center with high professional standards and a reputation for excellence. The best qualified candidate is student-centered, communicates clearly and effectively, is a team player, advocates for STEM, and is capable of working effectively with staff and faculty to serve the diverse needs of students. The Advanced Academic Advisor builds upon the foundational role of the Academic Advisor, offering deeper expertise in academic planning, student engagement, and retention strategies. This position focuses on providing enhanced advising services to specialized student populations, including transfer students, at-risk students, and those in specific academic disciplines. The Advanced Advisor works closely with faculty and administrative staff to ensure that students meet academic goals and are on track for graduation. The role also includes involvement in professional development and special projects that contribute to the overall success of the advising center. Perform related tasks and special projects as assigned. Note: a flexible work schedule is required to accommodate student requests for advising after traditional work hours. Required Education Advisor: Master’s degree (earned by start date). A Bachelor's Degree and three (3) years of directly relevant work experience will be considered in lieu of a Master’s degree. Advanced Advisor: Master's degree (earned by start date) in a related field is required. Required Related Experience Advisor: No experience required with a Master's degree. Advanced Advisor: Minimum of two years of experience in the role of Academic Advisor. Documents Needed to Apply Cover Letter & Resume Required MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee and their spouse and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email hrs@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: For best consideration, please apply by December 7, 2026.  Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and the position may be filled before the listed application review date of September 11, 2026. Recommended Jobs Maintenance Supervisor - TN Miller Coliseum Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Facilities Services - Maintenance, Other Perform a variety of repair and preventative maintenance tasks including electrical, plumbing, HVAC, carpentry, metal fabrication, and masonry for the Tennessee Miller Coliseum. Operate HVAC system controls to ensure appropriate cooling or heating of indoor spaces. Arrange and oversee maintenance service from external contractors or other university departments. Train, schedule, and supervise part-time maintenance staff. Perform other tasks as assigned. Administrative Assistant 3 - Joey A. Jacobs Chair of Excellence in Accounting Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Administrative/Clerical Support, College of Business The Administrative Assistant 3 provides comprehensive administrative, operational, and event-planning support to the Joey A. Jacobs Chair of Excellence in Accounting within the Department of Accounting at Middle Tennessee State University (MTSU). The position helps advance the Chair’s mission of promoting leadership in accounting education, professional engagement, student development, and outreach through programs, events, and collaborations with internal and external stakeholders.\n\nKey responsibilities include planning and coordinating conferences, workshops, meetings, and special events; assisting with marketing and promotional activities; managing social media communications; arranging travel, catering, room reservations, and event logistics; and coordinating the selection and ordering of awards, gifts, promotional items, and memorabilia. The role also maintains records, registrations, rosters, and electronic files; prepares reports and correspondence; and provides administrative support for academic and program initiatives.\n\nThe position serves as a central point of contact for the Jacobs Chair, working closely with faculty, students, Beta Alpha Psi, professional accounting organizations, industry representatives, government agencies, educational institutions, and other partners. Responsibilities include facilitating communications, coordinating activities among stakeholders, addressing operational issues, and supporting initiatives that increase the visibility and impact of MTSU’s accounting program. The Administrative Assistant also assists with academic and administrative processes and performs other duties necessary to support the goals and activities of the Jacobs Chair of Excellence. Executive Assistant -  Jones College of Business Advising Center Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Administrative/Clerical Support, College of Business The Jones College of Business at Middle Tennessee State University invites applications for an Executive Assistant in the Undergraduate Advising Center. This position serves as a key member of the advising team and provides comprehensive administrative, operational, and student support services that contribute to student success, retention, and timely degree completion.\n\nThe Executive Assistant serves as the primary point of contact for students, prospective students, parents, faculty, staff, and campus partners interacting with the Undergraduate Advising Center. Responsibilities include coordinating advising appointments, managing high-volume student communications, assisting with registration and graduation processes, maintaining student records, supporting advising initiatives, processing employment documents in the hiring verification workflow, and helping students navigate university policies and procedures.\n\nThe position also supports the daily operations of the Advising Center through office management, event coordination, communication and outreach efforts, data reporting, purchasing, scheduling, and technology support. The Executive Assistant assists with planning and implementing orientation programs, recruitment activities, advising workshops, and other student success initiatives while maintaining confidentiality and ensuring compliance with university policies and FERPA regulations.\n\nThe successful candidate will possess excellent organizational, communication, customer service, and problem-solving skills; the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment; and experience using technology and information systems to support student services. This position plays an important role in fostering a welcoming, student-centered environment and advancing the mission of the Jones College Undergraduate Advising Center. © 2026 Middle Tennessee State University Cookie Preferences Nondiscrimination Policy Terms Follow Us: Facebook LinkedIn X Instagra