    "https://careers.mtsu.edu/jobs/systems-analyst-2-murfreesboro-tennessee-tennessee-united-states-061fb333-0b6c-446f-97e3-97c1171085c7": {
      "title": "Systems Analyst 2",
      "description": "Systems Analyst 2 - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Visit MTSU Why Choose MTSU Applicant Log In My Profile Kiosk mode Systems Analyst 2 498640 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Information Technology Administrative Add to favorites View favorites Job Title Systems Analyst 2 Department Admin Information Systems Services Salary Commensurate with experience Job Summary/Basic Function The role of Systems Analyst 2 is to maintain data integrity and ensure the smooth operation of the Enterprise Application systems and integrations with third-party applications. This position will collaborate closely with end-users, monitor business processes, and offer innovative solutions to enhance administrative functions that support students, faculty, staff, alumni, and the institution's broader objectives. The Systems Analyst 2 will contribute to the overall business improvement process, exhibit excellent troubleshooting, diagnostic, and decision-making skills, and possess a thorough understanding of programming, database, and API concepts and design. Duties and Responsibilities include but are not limited to, maintaining data integrity to ensure efficient Enterprise Application operations and integrations with third-party systems; collaborating closely with end-users to gather requirements, design, test, and implement computer information systems, software applications, integrations, reports, dashboards, and process improvements that support the institution’s goals; monitoring and assessing the quality of technical and functional business processes to identify data-related issues, and provide effective resolutions; conducting feasibility studies of programming requests and provide technical guidance to customers on programming issues; assisting operations staff in troubleshooting and resolving system-related problems; coordinating the installation of patches and upgrades with database administrators, system support teams, and functional users; maintaining expertise in the institution's enterprise applications, reporting techniques, and relevant business procedures; serving as a knowledgeable resource to guide and train other Systems Analysts on business processes, data usage, system integration, and cross-system dependencies; acting as a liaison between technical teams and user departments to ensure smooth communication and collaboration; and contributing continuously to business improvement initiatives. ITD is seeking a qualified candidate to provide technical support for the Finance, Accounts Receivable, and Document Management systems and business functions. Required Education Associate degree or bachelor's degree (experience requirements for each degree are in the Required Related Experience section) Required Related Experience Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, or related field: Two (2) years of relevant experience is required. Bachelor's degree in any field: Three (3) years of relevant experience is required. Associate's degree in any field: Four (4) years of relevant experience is required. Relevant experience earned as a graduate assistant or student worker may be considered. Desirable Related Experience Experience working in higher education administrative programming. Experience providing technical support to Ellucian Banner. Experience providing technical support to Oracle ERP, HCM, and EPM Cloud Applications. Documents Needed to Apply Resume Required MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee and their spouse and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email hrs@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: For best consideration, please apply by July 28, 2026.  Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and the position may be filled before the listed application review date of November 13, 2026. Back to search results Apply Now First Name (required) 82a9a67c Last Name (required) d703619c Email (required) 60ae9bb1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Academic Advisor/Advanced Academic Advisor -  College of Basic and Applied Sciences (CBAS) Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Academic Advising , College of Basic & Applied Sciences The College of Basic and Applied Sciences (CBAS) at Middle Tennessee State University invites applications for an Academic Advisor/Advanced Academic Advisor position in the following departments: Department of Aerospace, School of Agriculture, Department of Chemistry and Pre-Professional Health Sciences, Department of Computational and Data Science, and the School of Concrete and Construction Management. The Academic Advisor will collaborate with students to co-create educational plans in ways that are consistent with their aspirations, interests, strengths, and values--preparing them for a life of learning in a diverse and global society. MTSU Academic Advising fosters a collaborative, holistic, and inclusive student-centered relationship that promotes academic and personal growth so students can thrive in the University community. Through innovative, transformative, and informed practice, Academic Advisors empower students to think critically and take ownership of their journey and success. Academic Advisors work with traditional, transfer, undeclared, and pre-professional health students, ensuring they stay on track for graduation through constant engagement and monitoring. The Academic Advisor role is geared toward supporting student success, providing both academic and career advising while maintaining high standards of professionalism and collaboration within their respective college. CBAS has an established Advising Center with high professional standards and a reputation for excellence. The best qualified candidate is student-centered, communicates clearly and effectively, is a team player, advocates for STEM, and is capable of working effectively with staff and faculty to serve the diverse needs of students.\n\nThe Advanced Academic Advisor builds upon the foundational role of the Academic Advisor, offering deeper expertise in academic planning, student engagement, and retention strategies. This position focuses on providing enhanced advising services to specialized student populations, including transfer students, at-risk students, and those in specific academic disciplines. The Advanced Advisor works closely with faculty and administrative staff to ensure that students meet academic goals and are on track for graduation. The role also includes involvement in professional development and special projects that contribute to the overall success of the advising center. Perform related tasks and special projects as assigned. Note: a flexible work schedule is required to accommodate student requests for advising after traditional work hours. Maintenance Supervisor - TN Miller Coliseum Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Facilities Services - Maintenance, Other Perform a variety of repair and preventative maintenance tasks including electrical, plumbing, HVAC, carpentry, metal fabrication, and masonry for the Tennessee Miller Coliseum. Operate HVAC system controls to ensure appropriate cooling or heating of indoor spaces. Arrange and oversee maintenance service from external contractors or other university departments. Train, schedule, and supervise part-time maintenance staff. Perform other tasks as assigned. Administrative Assistant 3 - Joey A. Jacobs Chair of Excellence in Accounting Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Administrative/Clerical Support, College of Business The Administrative Assistant 3 provides comprehensive administrative, operational, and event-planning support to the Joey A. Jacobs Chair of Excellence in Accounting within the Department of Accounting at Middle Tennessee State University (MTSU). The position helps advance the Chair’s mission of promoting leadership in accounting education, professional engagement, student development, and outreach through programs, events, and collaborations with internal and external stakeholders.\n\nKey responsibilities include planning and coordinating conferences, workshops, meetings, and special events; assisting with marketing and promotional activities; managing social media communications; arranging travel, catering, room reservations, and event logistics; and coordinating the selection and ordering of awards, gifts, promotional items, and memorabilia. The role also maintains records, registrations, rosters, and electronic files; prepares reports and correspondence; and provides administrative support for academic and program initiatives.\n\nThe position serves as a central point of contact for the Jacobs Chair, working closely with faculty, students, Beta Alpha Psi, professional accounting organizations, industry representatives, government agencies, educational institutions, and other partners. Responsibilities include facilitating communications, coordinating activities among stakeholders, addressing operational issues, and supporting initiatives that increase the visibility and impact of MTSU’s accounting program. The Administrative Assistant also assists with academic and administrative processes and performs other duties necessary to support the goals and activities of the Jacobs Chair of Excellence. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert a6417f56 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Information Technology Information Technology Employment Type Administrative Administrative Locations Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States First Name (required) 43170977 Last Name (required) b067a821 Email (required) 6a1c8683 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Middle Tennessee State University Cookie Preferences Nondiscrimination Policy Terms Follow Us: Facebook LinkedIn X Instagram Youtube Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
